<p>LOOKING AHEAD →</p>
<p>Aristotle has an account of what the good life looks like (eudaimonia) and what the parts of that life are (the virtues). The obvious next question is about responsibility. If virtue is acquired through habituation, and habituation depends on circumstances we do not always choose, when are we actually on the hook for what we do? That is Book III.</p>
